session:pr768Summary a agp:TranscriptSummary ;
    agp:summaryText "Issue #742 asked for a reader counterpart to sparql_json.rs's existing to_sparql_json serializer, needed by SPARQL SERVICE federation (#741) to parse a remote endpoint's results JSON back into solution bindings. Chose Vec<SolutionRow> (sparql_parser's existing HashMap<String, GraphElement> row type) as the output rather than inventing a new type, since it's already the resolved-term row shape used elsewhere in the crate. The main design question was blank nodes: rather than parsing a bnode label like \"b0\" back into RdfResource::AnonymousBlankNode's numeric id (which would both reject arbitrary remote labels like \"genid-x\" and risk colliding with locally-interned bnode ids), each from_sparql_json call keeps its own label->GraphElement map and allocates a fresh anonymous node per distinct label via Datastore::new_anonymous_blank_node, giving correct per-document scoping. Triple terms (RDF 1.2, type:\"triple\") do need &mut Datastore after all, confirmed by reading TripleTermKey/Datastore::add_triple_term: its fields are interned GraphElementIds, not inline GraphElements, so each component is interned via add_resource before building the TripleTermKey. For literals, gave dedicated parsing to the fixed XSD set the serializer emits (boolean/integer/decimal/float/double/dateTime/date/time/duration) to preserve round-trip fidelity, falling back to RdfLiteral::TypedLiteral both for unrecognized datatypes and for any recognized datatype whose lexical form fails to parse (ill-typed RDF literals are legal). Along the way found that literal_to_json's own DurationLiteral encoding uses {:?} (Debug) instead of ISO 8601, so it cannot actually round-trip through any correct duration parser; left that serializer bug unfixed (out of this issue's scope) and filed it as a separate follow-up issue rather than silently working around it in prose." ;
    agp:reasoningFor ghpull:768 ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy session:pr768 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo session:claudeSonnet5 .
